"""mr-residual-history — read-only views of the residual registry for planning and the drain.

Never writes anything. The registry (mr-residuals.jsonl) is folded with mr-gates' own
`fold_residuals`/`open_residuals` (loaded from the mr-gates file beside this one), so open/closed
means exactly what `mr-gates residuals list` means.

  mr-residual-history related --paths P[,P...] [--json]
      For milestone elaboration (milestone-loop-prompt.md, residual pre-mortem). Rows whose cited
      paths overlap P (a path matches a P that is equal to it or a directory prefix of it):
        open     — fold candidates (see milestone-loop-prompt.md's pre-mortem for which ones)
        closed   — the defect classes earlier work on these files produced, counted by category
      A P may be a glob (`client/src/main.*.test.ts`, `client/src/**`): it matches from its
      literal prefix up to the first `*`.
  mr-residual-history sort [--json]
      For the residual review (mr-residual-review-playbook.md). Every open row, with:
        paths    — cited paths: the row's `touches` plus repo paths named in its title/reason
        state    — unchanged: no cited path changed on origin since the row was filed (still real;
                              no re-check needed)
                   changed:   a cited path changed since (possibly fixed; check it)
                   gone:      no cited path exists on origin any more (check where it went)
                   no-paths:  nothing cited (check it)
        reviewed — the latest rv verdict on the row (`residual-reviews/*.verdicts.json`) and its
                   date, or null; `recheck` is false when that verdict still stands (no cited path
                   changed since) so a review does not re-read it
        named_in — spec files that already name the row's id (owned there; never clustered again)
        followup — the row came from a follow-up slice (mr-gates' rule: it may not be promoted)
        cluster  — category + the leading two path components, for grouping fixes
  mr-residual-history --selftest
Paths resolve against origin/master of the game checkout, then origin/main of the harness.
ALWAYS exits 0 except a --selftest failure (rc 1).
"""
